The current solution only tries **moves** in the local search. Adding **swap** moves (exchanging a model on the worst GPU with one on another GPU) can escape configurations where no single move helps, further reducing max KVPR while keeping the code simple and fast.

I'll extend `_refine` to also try swaps between the worst-KVPR GPU and every other GPU.

